		"Sunlord:L_Sunlord_AMWPH4018_4x4x1.8mm": {
			"assembly": {
				"dist_part_numbers": [
					"C2846183"
				],
				"mpn": "AMWPH4018S2R2MT",
				"package": "SMD 4.0x4.0x1.8mm"
			},
			"bless": null,
			"converter_version": null,
			"layer": "seed",
			"license": "LicenseRef-TurnRock-Proprietary",
			"model3d_ref": null,
			"original_source_path": null,
			"path": "Sunlord.pretty/L_Sunlord_AMWPH4018_4x4x1.8mm.kicad_mod",
			"provenance_note": "smart-remote v2 rev B: L1 buck inductor, replacing the Vishay-named land. Pads 1.8 x 3.7 at +/-1.5 span x 0.6 to 2.4 against a terminal at 0.9 to 2.0 - 0.3 inboard and 0.4 outboard, where the fillet forms. NOTE the old Inductor_SMD:L_Vishay_IFSC-1515AH land (1.15 wide at +/-1.475, spanning 0.9 to 2.05) covers the termination but gives far less fillet than Sunlord specifies; an earlier 'verified drop-in, no board change' assessment of it rested on the swapped a/b reading and was wrong. Non-polar, nothing on F.Fab past the body outline, anchor (0, 0).",
			"retrieved_at": "2026-08-31",
			"sha256": "56975c0fbf8789718eeca64f2082daa03517f45766fe9de98e1248611edfeb74",
			"size_bytes": 3086,
			"source_kind": "hand_authored",
			"source_ref": "authored 2026-08-31 from the Sunlord AMWPH4018S series datasheet, Fig.3-1 and Table 3-1: A=B=4.0, C=1.8, D=3.3, E=1.1, a=1.2, b=1.8, c=3.7. READ THE FIGURE: 'a' is the GAP BETWEEN PADS and 'b' is EACH PAD'S WIDTH, not the other way round. Both orderings give the same +/-1.5 centres, so the arithmetic self-checks either way and a swap is invisible - it was caught only by zooming into Fig.3-1 and seeing which edges the extension lines drop from. Verified in KiCad 9.0.9 and 10.0.5."
		},
		"Syntiant:SPK0641HT4H-1_TopPort_LGA-8_4x3mm": {
			"assembly": {
				"dist_part_numbers": [
					"C5159510"
				],
				"mpn": "SPK0641HT4H-1",
				"package": "LGA-8 4.0x3.0x1.0mm"
			},
			"bless": null,
			"converter_version": null,
			"layer": "seed",
			"license": "LicenseRef-TurnRock-Proprietary",
			"model3d_ref": null,
			"original_source_path": null,
			"path": "Syntiant.pretty/SPK0641HT4H-1_TopPort_LGA-8_4x3mm.kicad_mod",
			"provenance_note": "smart-remote v2 rev B: U3 microphone, replacing MEMSensing:MSM261S4030H0R_TopPort_LGA-8_4x3mm. TOP PORT so no PCB acoustic hole. SAME body and footprint name shape as the MSM261 but a DIFFERENT pinout - pad 8 is GROUND here and was +3V3 on the MSM261 layout, so reusing the old net map shorts the mic rail. PDM output, not I2S: pad 1 DATA, pad 2 CLOCK. Pad 3 SELECT is internally pulled low (left channel); tie it to GND to make that explicit. Pads 5-8 are all GROUND. The CPL rotation for this land is now MEASURED, not assumed: pcb/library/part_orientation.json records our drawing as the vendor's (LCSC C5159510) turned 180 deg counter-clockwise. It has still not been verified against an assembled board. The F.Fab pin-1 marker sits INSIDE the body outline on purpose: the compiler takes its anchor from the fab extent first (assembly_anchor), so a marker poking past the outline would shift every placed part - it measured -0.0925mm in x before this was corrected.",
			"retrieved_at": "2026-08-31",
			"sha256": "1c032df0f80e277f26dfc85e1e7691b88618757e7333bb281a16344a57b1a64e",
